  "summary": "The Sky Tower in Auckland, New Zealand, is a 328-metre concrete tower. Work began in 1994 and it was inaugurated on 3 August 1997, about two years and nine months after construction started. The AA describes it as the tallest freestanding structure in the southern hemisphere, and its shaft has an internal diameter of 12 metres.",
